### Works in IntelliJ's HTTP client (or copy the calls into Postman).
### 1. Register, then paste the accessToken into @token below.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Test","lastName":"User","email":"test@example.com","password":"password123"}

###
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Categories (seeded: ids 1-4 are INCOME, 5-12 are EXPENSE)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/categories?type=EXPENSE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add income
POST http://localhost:8080/api/income
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"categoryId":1,"amount":15000.00,"description":"October salary","incomeDate":"2026-10-25"}

### Add expense
POST http://localhost:8080/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"categoryId":5,"amount":250.50,"paymentMethod":"CARD","description":"Groceries","expenseDate":"2026-10-26"}

### Search expenses
GET http://localhost:8080/api/expenses?q=groc&from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Income category used on an expense -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"categoryId":1,"amount":10,"expenseDate":"2026-10-26"}

### Amount of zero -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"categoryId":5,"amount":0,"expenseDate":"2026-10-26"}
